<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moghulistan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moghulistan was the eastern successor state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Empire</a>, based on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ili-river">Ili River</a> steppe. After the Timurid conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> in the fourteenth century, it remained the surviving Chagataid realm. It survived in diminished form for another century, often dominated by tribal leaders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moghulistan.jpg" alt="Moghulistan" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ro4444 at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chagatai_Khanate_(1490).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
